 "description": "Dry glass reptile terrarium (vivarium) for a captive snake: black frame, grey mesh lid with a dome heat lamp on the right (orange bulb glow inside), warm cream back wall, sand floor with speckles, grey-brown rock at left, dry branch at left, small grey water dish at right, dry grass tuft, glass glare. NO water fill, fish, bubbles or coral. Same footprint as `aquarium`. Anchor = bottom-centre; glass x -290..+290, y -372..0 (lid to -392, lamp top -500). Clear middle x -90..+180, y -300..-70 holds `inland_taipan` at about 0.45-0.5 scale (place it at tank x, y = tank y - 110 x tank scale).",
